Introduction

At CLINE APC, we prioritize your privacy. This Privacy Policy outlines the personal information we collect, how we utilize it, and the choices available to you regarding our use of your information.

Information We Collect

We gather personal information when you visit our website, complete forms on our site, or contact us via email, phone, or in person. This information may include your name, address, email address, phone number, and any additional details you provide.

We also collect non-personal information about your interaction with our website through cookies. Cookies are small text files placed on your device during your visit. They help us remember your preferences and recognize your device during subsequent visits.

How We Use Your Information

We may use your personal information to respond to your inquiries, provide legal services, send newsletters or marketing materials, and comply with legal requirements. Additionally, we use your information to enhance our website and services, and to personalize your experience with us.

Cookies help us improve our website’s functionality and tailor your experience. They allow us to remember your preferences, recognize your device on future visits, analyze website usage, and monitor user activity.

Sharing Your Information

We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties. However, we may share your information with third-party service providers who assist in operating our website or delivering legal services. We may also disclose your information to comply with legal obligations or protect our rights.

Security of Your Information

We implement reasonable measures to safeguard your personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure, or alteration. Despite these efforts, no method of internet transmission or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

Your Choices

You have the option to opt-out of receiving marketing materials from us by contacting us at the address provided below. You may also request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information by reaching out to us.

You can manage cookie use through your web browser settings. You can opt to be notified when cookies are being placed on your device or choose to block cookies entirely. However, blocking cookies may limit your ability to use certain features of our website.

Changes to Our Privacy Policy

We reserve the right to modify this Privacy Policy at any time without prior notice. Your continued use of our website and services after any changes indicates your acceptance of the updated policy.

If you have any questions or concerns about our Privacy Policy or how we handle your personal information, please contact us at:

